      "location": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-13-ma-markowitz-upper-preparation.md:39-43; MA-MARKOWITZ-UPPER-CONTRACT.md Arithmetic and eligibility",
      "title": "Guard speculative diagonal lookup before checking row eligibility",
      "detail": "The scalar diagonal argument and finite-diagonal precheck imply an eager diagonal[pivot] read, although the original source reads it only after all row arithmetic. For a malformed shortened diagonal and a two-term rational row whose first product is zero times infinity, original gmp.jl mul! throws DivideError before the diagonal lookup; eager eligibility lookup instead throws BoundsError. An in-bounds unassigned diagonal can similarly throw UndefRefError too early. This contradicts the broad malformed-input exception/publication parity requirement.",
      "fix": "Pass diagonal vector and pivot to eligibility. Check checkbounds(Bool,diagonal,pivot) and isassigned(diagonal,pivot) before reading it; false must run the exact original loop and its later diagonal lookup. Add combined-error regressions for absent and unassigned diagonal with earlier zero-times-infinity rational arithmetic. Keep generic loop and publication order unchanged."
    }
